  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Two volunteers can answer collection questions or welcome arrivals during a short service period.\", \"decision\": \"How should volunteers divide interpretation and reception?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nEach volunteer welcomes a small group at reception and continues with its interpretation questions. Visitors can keep the same contact through the beginning of the visit.\nThe volunteers exchange reception and interpretation roles halfway through the service period. Both share the roles while retaining clear assignments.\nOne volunteer handles reception and the other interpretation for the entire service period. Each maintains continuity in one role."
    }
  ],
